<title>USA: Gabelli cuts Bay Meadows stake to 6.08 pct.</title>
<headline>Gabelli cuts Bay Meadows stake to 6.08 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investor Mario Gabelli said Tuesday it cut its stake in Bay Meadows Operating Co to 350,400 common shares, or 6.08 percent of the total outstanding, from 408,300 shares, or 7.08 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold 57,900 shares between Sept. 3 and Oct. 11 at prices ranging from $18.375 to $24.098 a share.</p>
<p>Shares of Bay Meadows trade under a pairing agreement with California Jockey Club, a real estate investment trust, as a single unit.</p>
